/*!
\page page_stFtpcHit StFtpcHit

\brief Reconstructed hit in the STAR Forward Time Projection Chamber (FTPC).

\ref StFtpcHit represents a single reconstructed cluster in the STAR Forward TPC (FTPC). The
FTPC is a cylindrical TPC along the beam axis covering 2.5 < |η| < 4, with an East and a West
module. Hits are produced from \c StFtpcPoint objects by the FTPC cluster finder and stored in
\ref StFtpcHitCollection. In addition to the inherited position and charge, \ref StFtpcHit stores
the cluster centroid and its uncertainty in native pad and time-bin coordinates.

\section sec_ftpchit_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\verbatim
TObject
└── StObject
    └── StMeasuredPoint
        └── StHit
            └── StFtpcHit        (concrete — this class)
\endverbatim

Objects are held in \c StSPtrVecFtpcHit inside \ref StFtpcHitCollection, owned by the StEvent
framework.

\section sec_ftpchit_hwpack Hardware Address Packing (mHardwarePosition)

| Bits | Width | Meaning | Accessor |
|---|---|---|---|
| 0–3 | 4 | StDetectorId (kFtpcEastId=5 or kFtpcWestId=4) | detector() |
| 4–8 | 5 | Readout plane number (1–20) | plane() |
| 9–11 | 3 | Sector number (1–6) | sector() |
| 12–19 | 8 | Number of pads in cluster | padsInHit() |
| 20–28 | 9 | Number of time bins in cluster | timebinsInHit() |

\section sec_ftpchit_members Data Members

\subsection subsec_ftpchit_inherited Inherited (selected)
- <tt>UInt_t mHardwarePosition</tt> — Packed FTPC hardware address (see table above).
- <tt>StThreeVectorF mPosition</tt> — 3-D hit centroid in STAR global frame (cm).
- <tt>StThreeVectorF mPositionError</tt> — 1-sigma position uncertainties (cm).
- <tt>Float_t mCharge</tt> — Cluster charge encoded as
  <tt>float(ftpcq) / 65536.0</tt> where \c ftpcq is the integer charge from the FTPC cluster
  finder.
- <tt>UChar_t mFlag</tt> — FTPC cluster status flags.

\subsection subsec_ftpchit_own StFtpcHit-specific
- <tt>Float_t mPadPos</tt> — Hit centroid in pad units within the FTPC readout plane.
- <tt>Float_t mTimePos</tt> — Hit centroid in time-bin units within the FTPC drift window.
- <tt>Float_t mPadPosSigma</tt> — Standard deviation of the pad position (pad units).
- <tt>Float_t mTimePosSigma</tt> — Standard deviation of the time-bin position (time-bin units).

\section sec_ftpchit_methods Key Methods

- <tt>StDetectorId detector() const</tt> — Returns \c kFtpcEastId (5) or \c kFtpcWestId (4)
  from bits 0–3 of the hardware position.
- <tt>unsigned int sector() const</tt> — Sector 1–6 (bits 9–11).
- <tt>unsigned int plane() const</tt> — Readout plane 1–20 (bits 4–8).
- <tt>unsigned int padsInHit() const</tt> — Number of pads in cluster (bits 12–19).
- <tt>unsigned int timebinsInHit() const</tt> — Number of time bins in cluster (bits 20–28).
- <tt>double padPosition() const</tt> — Centroid in pad units (\c mPadPos).
- <tt>double timePosition() const</tt> — Centroid in time-bin units (\c mTimePos).
- <tt>double sigmaPadPosition() const</tt> — Pad position sigma.
- <tt>double sigmaTimePosition() const</tt> — Time position sigma.
- <tt>void setPadPosition(float)</tt>, <tt>setTimePosition(float)</tt>,
  <tt>setSigmaPadPosition(float)</tt>, <tt>setSigmaTimePosition(float)</tt> — Setters.
- <tt>void update(const StFtpcPoint&)</tt> — Re-populates all fields from an
  \c StFtpcPoint cluster object.

\section sec_ftpchit_ownership Object Ownership

\ref StFtpcHit uses a custom memory pool (\c StMemoryPool) via overloaded \c new/delete. Objects
are owned by \ref StFtpcHitCollection. <b>Do not delete StFtpcHit* pointers from a collection.</b>

\section sec_ftpchit_usage Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
StFtpcHitCollection* ftpcColl = event->ftpcHitCollection();
if (!ftpcColl) return;

for (const StFtpcHit* hit : ftpcColl->hits()) {
    bool isEast = (hit->detector() == kFtpcEastId);
    std::cout << (isEast ? "E" : "W")
              << " sec=" << hit->sector()
              << " plane=" << hit->plane()
              << " pad=" << hit->padPosition()
              << " t=" << hit->timePosition()
              << " q=" << hit->charge() << "\n";
}
\endcode

\sa \ref page_sthit, \ref page_stmeasuredpoint, \ref page_stFtpcHitCollection
*/
